{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CrossingGradedMassExpansion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CrossingGradedMassExpansion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.mass_at_zero_depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.mass_at_zero_depth","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L99-L142","doc":"Classical-limit recovery: at zero depth, the total mass equals\nthe Gröbner-Shirshov mass.  This is the substantive recovery\nstatement: at `(depth k).value = 0`, the expansion collapses\nto its `n = 0` term, which by `gbCoeffZero_eq_groebner` is\nthe GB mass.\n\nProof: substitute `h` into `expansion`; the Horner foldl with\n`acc * 0 + gbCoeff k n = gbCoeff k n` becomes a constant-update\nfoldl, so its value on the reversed range is `gbCoeff k`\napplied to the range's last element, which is `0`.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] Ch 11 §8 / crossing-graded-mass-expansion ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.expansion","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Horner-form expansion: evaluates the depth polynomial in\nO(c) multiplications, numerically more stable than the\nnaive power-based sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.gbCoeffZero_eq_groebner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.gbCoeffZero_eq_groebner","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L50-L50","doc":"At `n = 0`, the graded coefficient IS the Gröbner-Shirshov\nmass (definitional; connects the abstract grading to the\nexisting GB pipeline). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.groebnerMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.groebnerMass","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The standard Gröbner-Shirshov mass — an independent datum\nprovided per instance, used to anchor the `n = 0` term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.mass","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.gbCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.gbCoeff","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.depth","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.crossingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.crossingCount","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CrossingGradedMassExpansion","kind":"class","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L35-L58","doc":"**Crossing-graded mass expansion** (conjectural class).\nPackages the claim that the categorical mass of an atomic\nlink has the perturbative expansion indexed by subsets of\nlifted crossings. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:crossing-graded-mass-expansion","label":"conj:crossing-graded-mass-expansion","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.DepthScalar.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.DepthScalar.value","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.DepthScalar.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.DepthScalar.mk","kind":"ctor","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L32-L32","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.DepthScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.DepthScalar","kind":"structure","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/crossing-graded-mass-expansion.lean#L28-L33","doc":"Per-crossing universal depth scalar.  In the paper,\nξ(q) = D(λ(ℰ_q)) / ℏ_q², where D is the Bloch-Wigner\ndilogarithm and λ the Legendre invariant of the Descartes\nelliptic curve.  Here kept abstract. ","signatureChunk":0}]}